; High-priority exception policy zone (trusted order is fixed in
; config.json).  PASSTHRU here overrides any lower-priority block.
;
; RPZ QNAME trigger owners are written relative to the policy zone origin,
; i.e. "allowed.wild.example" denotes the data name allowed.wild.example.
$ORIGIN exception.rpz.
$TTL 3600

@                       SOA ns1.example. hostmaster.example. (
                                2026111800 3600 900 86400 3600 )
@                       NS  ns1.example.

; QNAME exception: exact allow for one host under a wildcard block.
allowed.wild.example    CNAME rpz-passthru.

; QNAME exception: exact allow that beats the lower-zone wildcard.
special.evil.example    CNAME rpz-passthru.

; Response-address exception for a single IPv4 address (203.0.113.254/32).
32.254.113.0.203.rpz-ip CNAME rpz-passthru.
